  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If NDI output  is introduced to VRChat, it could greatly enhance live broadcasting for content events, especially when combined with tools like Dolly cameras or drone cameras. Here’s why:\n\nReal-time Multi-Angle Coverage: NDI enables seamless streaming of multiple camera feeds over a network, allowing creators to capture diverse perspectives in VRChat worlds and events.\n\nDrone Camera Integration: Using drone cameras with NDI would provide unique aerial views, enriching the visual experience for live broadcasts.\n\nOptimized Streaming for YouTube: NDI’s compatibility with platforms like OBS simplifies high-quality streaming to YouTube, making it ideal for professional content creators.\n\nOverall, combining NDI with creative camera setups in VRChat opens up new possibilities for immersive and professional live event coverage.\n\nIf NDI is implemented in VRChat, it could enable the use of new features for real-time streaming. These features might include:\n\nIndividual Source Streaming: Specific elements like avatars, backgrounds, or audio could be streamed as separate NDI sources, allowing creators to mix and edit these elements in real time using external software like OBS or vMix.\n\nNetwork-Based Collaboration: Multiple users on the same network could share and manage NDI sources collaboratively, making team-based event production more efficient.\n\nUsers on other networks can use the NDI Bridge feature.\n\nEnhanced Platform Integration: With NDI's compatibility, VRChat content could be seamlessly integrated into platforms like YouTube or Twitch, as well as professional production tools, enabling advanced live-streaming workflows.\n\nThese features would expand the possibilities for content creators by offering greater flexibility and creative control in live-streaming VRChat events.\n\nThe NDI output feature is also used on Skype and Zoom.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_Device_Interface\n\nhttps://ndi.video/",
